NAME
    rotate - set the scene's rotation and redraw

SYNOPSIS
    rotate [x y z [px py pz]]

DESCRIPTION
    The geometry engine's record list survives between commands -- it IS
    the scene. Build one (tri, tri ... k, or cube's aftermath), then
    rotate it: this command rewrites only the engine's rotation matrix
    and redraws. Angles are in BRADS: 256 is a full turn, 64 is 90
    degrees, negative allowed. They apply as yaw (y), then pitch (x),
    then roll (z), about the PIVOT point -- the world origin unless you
    give one. The pivot matters: scenes live at z of a few hundred, and
    spinning them about the origin swings them out of the window; give
    the scene's own centre (0 0 400, say) and it turns in place. The
    command writes the whole transform (matrix and translation). With no
    arguments everything resets. Needs the engine.

EXAMPLES
    tri -80 -80 300 80 -80 300 0 40 420 f 31 0 0
    rotate 0 32 0 0 0 360     yaw an eighth-turn about the scene's middle
    rotate 16 32 0 0 0 360    ...pitched too
    rotate                    back to straight-on

SEE ALSO
    tri, cube, g3d
